    "ls|LS17_S11_U_298": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 298 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03RD FEBRUARY 2023 \n \nSUPER SPECIALITY HOSPITALS/BLOCKS UNDER PMSSY \n \n298.  SHRI KRUPAL BALAJI TUMANE: \nDR. DNV SENTHILKUMAR S.: \nSHRI ACHYUTANANDA SAMANTA: \n \nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government have sanctioned/ approved setting up of Super Speciality Blocks/ \nhospitals under Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Su raksha Yojana and if so, the details thereof along \nwith the present status of such blocks/hospitals, State/ UT -wise including Maharashtra, Tamil \nNadu, Odisha and in tribal and backward areas of the country; \n \n(b) the funds allocated by the Government in this regard; \n \n(c) whether there is a shortage of specialist doctors in the such Super Speciality Blocks/hospitals \nand if so, the details thereof and reaction of the Government thereto along with efforts made to \nmeet the requirements; \n \n(d) whether the Governme nt has also taken steps to establish Super Speciality Hospitals at par \nwith All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS), Delhi in other State/UTs including Tamil \nNadu and if so, the details of the action taken in this regard; and \n \n(e) the steps taken/proposed to be taken for setting up Medical colleges in tribal districts of the \ncountry including in Kandhamal Parliamentary Constituency of Odisha? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY \nWELFARE \n(DR. BHARATI PRAVIN PAWAR) \n \n(a) to (b):  Total 75 projects of upgradation of Government Medical Colleges/Institutions \n(GMCIs) have been approved under Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana ( PMSSY) for \nsetting up of Super Speciality Block (SSB)/Trauma Centre . The status of these projects \n\nState/UT-wise, including Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu, Odisha and in tribal and backward areas \nalong with approved cost of projects is at Annexure I.  \n(c): As per the PMSSY , operation and maintenance of the facilities created unde r the Scheme  \nincluding the creation of post and the recruitment of human resources is the responsibility of the \nState Government. \n(d): Under Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana, Union Cabinet has approved  setting up \nof 22 All India Institutes of Medical Sciences ( AIIMS) including one AIIMS at Madurai in \nTamil Nadu. These AIIMS are listed below; \nS.No. State/UT Name of AIIMS S.No. State/UT Name of AIIMS \n1. Andhra Pradesh AIIMS, Mangalagiri 12. Madhya \nPradesh \nAIIMS, Bhopal \n2. Assam AIIMS, Guwahati 13. Maharashtra AIIMS, Nagpur \n3. Bihar AIIMS, Patna 14. Odisha AIIMS, Bhubaneswar \n4. AIIMS, Darbhanga 15. Punjab AIIMS, Bathinda \n5. Chhattisgarh AIIMS, Raipur 16. Rajasthan AIIMS, Jodhpur \n6. Gujarat AIIMS, Rajkot 17. Tamil Nadu AIIMS, Madurai \n7. Haryana AIIMS, Rewari 18. Telangana AIIMS, Bibinagar \n8. Himachal Pradesh AIIMS, Bilaspur 19. Uttar Pradesh AIIMS, Raebareli \n9. Jammu & Kashmir AIIMS, Jammu 20. AIIMS, Gorakhpur \n10. AIIMS, Kashmir 21. Uttarakhand AIIMS, Rishikesh \n11. Jharkhand AIIMS, Deoghar 22. West Bengal AIIMS, Kalyani \n \n(e): This Ministry is also implementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme for 'Establishment of new \nMedical Colleges attached with existing district/referral hospitals', with preference to \nunderserved areas and aspirational districts, where there is no existing Government or private \nmedical college. Under three phases of this Scheme, a total of 157 medical colleges have been \napproved in the country. The list of such medical colleges including in tribal and b ackward areas \nis at Annexure-II. \n***** \n \n\nAnnexure-I \nStatus of 75 upgradation projects of GMCIs under PMSSY \n \nSl. No. \nName of the \nState \nName of the  \nGMC/ Institute \n \nApproved Cost of \nProject (Rs. In crore) \nStatus  \n Physical \nProgress \nin % \nCentral \nshare \nState \nshare \nTo