    "ls|LS17_S11_U_309": "  \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *309 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.03.2023 \n \nPROMOTION OF TEXTILE INDUSTRY \n \n*309. SHRI HAJI FAZLUR REHMAN: \n \n Will the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंत्री \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) the details of action plan being implemented by the Government to promote the textile industry in \nthe country;  \n \n(b) whether the textile industry in the country is facing crisis due to which the textile units are closing \ndown and employees are being retrenched;  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(d) whether the Government has started any scheme for the progress of weavers working in the textile \nindustry; and  \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र मंत्री (श्री पीयूष गोयल) \nMINISTER OF TEXTILES \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (e):-  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\n  \n \n \nStatement in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *309 for answer on 22.03.2023 by Shri Haji \nFazlur Rehman regarding Promotion of Textile Industry. \n \n(a) to (c): Government is implementing various schemes viz Production Linked Incentive (PLI) \nScheme, Pradhan Mantri Mega Integrated Textile Region and Apparel (PM MITRA), National Technical \nTextiles Mission (NTTM) , Scheme for Integrated Textile Parks (SITP), SAMARTH - The Scheme for \nCapacity Building in Textile Sector, Jute (ICARE - Improved Cultivation and Advanced Retting \nExercise), Integrated Processing Development Scheme (IPDS), Silk Samagra 2.0, Amended Technology \nUpgradation Fund Scheme (A -TUFS), National Handicraft Development Programme , Comprehensive \nHandicrafts Cluster Devel opment Scheme, Integrated Wool Development Programme etc. catering \nexclusively for promotion and development of textile sector in the country. Exports of Textiles & Apparel \nincluding Handicrafts has increased by 41%, growing from US$ 31,585 million in FY 2 020-21 to        \nUS$ 44,435 million in FY 2021-22. \n \n(d) & (e): In addition to the above schemes, the Government is implementing following schemes \nfor progress of weavers across the country: \n \n1. National Handloom Development Programme; \n2. Raw Material Supply Scheme; \n \nUnder the above schemes, financial assistance is provided to the eligible handloom \nagencies/weavers for raw materials, common infrastructure development, marketing of handloom \nproducts both in domestic and overseas markets, Weavers MUDRA Loans etc.  \n \n**** \n \n ",
