    "ls|LS17_S11_U_332": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI, \nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA \nREJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *  †332 \nANSWERED ON 23.03.2023 \nCADWM \n* †332    SHRI SANJAY JADHAV \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Command Area Development and Water Management Programme (CADWM) is \nbeing implemented in the country particularly in Pa rbhani Parliamentary Constituency of \nMaharashtra; \n(b) if so, the current status thereof; \n(c) the details of the funds allocated and utilized  along with the number of beneficiaries under the \nsaid programme during the last five years, State/UT and year-wise; \n(d) the details of the works done under the said pr ogramme in other districts, tehsils and towns of \nMaharashtra during the last five years; and \n(e) the steps being taken/proposed to be taken by t he Government to expedite and expand the works \nunder the said programme? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL )   \n(a) to (e) : A statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF STARRED QUESTION \nNO. *332 TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 23.03.2023 REGARDING “CADWM”. \n(a) Yes, Sir. The Command Area Development and Water Ma nagement programme (CADWM) is \nbeing implemented in the country, including in part s of Parbhani Parliamentary Constituency of \nMaharashtra. \n(b)  Presently, the CADWM Programme is being implemente d pari passu with the prioritized projects \nof Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana - Acceler ated Irrigation Benefits Programme (PMKSY-\nAIBP) under the PMKSY component of Har Khet Ko Pani  (HKKP) from 2015-16 onwards. \nCulturable Command Area (CCA) of 45.08 lakh hectares has been targeted under PMKSY-CADWM \nprogramme.  \nThere are 22 PMKSY-CADWM projects in Maharashtra. L ower Dudhna CADWM project \nbenefits the Parbhani Parliamentary Constituency of  Maharashtra. It has been included under \nCADWM programme with following features: \nTarget CCA                                                    30,000 ha  \nTotal cost                                                   Rs.145 crore  \nCentral Assistance (CA) component          Rs.72 cr ore \nCA Release (From 2016-17 to 2021-22)     Rs 20 cror e  \nPhysical progress in CCA till March 2022   20,500 h a \n \n(c)    Under the PMKSY-CADWM, the year wise details of CA released and expenditure incurred for \nthe various State/UTs is provided at Annexure-I. Data on beneficiaries is not maintained in the \nMinistry. \n(d)    For the 22 projects of Maharashtra under PMKSY-C ADWM, the details of district/tehsils/towns \nbenefitted as well as physical and financial target s/progress projects of Maharashtra are given in the  \nAnnexure-II . \n(e)   To expedite and expand the works under CADWM Prog ramme, project monitoring is done \nregularly. This includes- \n1. The assessment of progress done through monitoring visits undertaken by CWC field offices \n(CAD Cells) and by Project Monitoring Unit (PMU) es tablished in the Ministry in respect of \nPMKSY;  \n2. Monitoring the progress of projects through online CADWM-Information System portal;  \n3. Reviewing the implementation of projects through ‘P roject Implementation Review Committee \n(PIRC)’ meetings held periodically; and  \n4. Reviews of program implementation undertaken in Ministry of Jal Shakti. \n*** \n\n  \n\nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (c) OF LOK SA BHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *332  TO BE ANSWERED ON \n23.03.2023“CADWM”.\nState-Wise  & Year-wise Central Assistance  released and Expenditure incurred under CADWM (PMKSY) Programme during  2016-17 to 2021-22 \nRs. in Crore  \nSr. \nNo. \nName of the \nState \nCentral Assistance Expenditure \n2016-17  2017-18  2018-19  2019-20  2020-\n21 \n2021-\n22 Total 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-\n20 \n2020-\n21 \n2021-\n22 Total \n1   Andhra \nPrade