    "ls|LS17_S11_U_342": "������������������� �\n��������������������������������������� �\n��\n��������� �\n�� ����������������������� �\n���������������������������� ��\n��\n������������������������������ �\n�\n���������������������������� �\n��\n���������������������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n���� �������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������� �����������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ���� ������������������� ���� ������ �������������\n����������������������������������������������������\n���� ���� �������� ��� ���� ������ ���������� ���� ��������� ������ ���� ����� ���������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������\n��\n������ �\n��\n���������������������� ����������������� �\n���������� ������������������� �\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������� ���� ���� ��������� ������ ����������� ����� ���� ���������� ����� ��������������� ���\n����������\n��\n�������� ������������������ ������ �������������������������� ���� �������������������� �������������������� �������������� �������������� ������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����� ���� ��� ���������� �������������� ���������� ������ �������� �������� ��� ������ ����������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������� ������� ���������������������� ������������� ����������� ������� ��� �����������\n���������� ������������ ������� ������ ������������ ����� ��� ���� ���� ������� ������������\n�������� ��� ������������ ����������������� ������ ���� ������ ��� ���������� ���� ����\n�������������� ����� ��� ��������� ��� ����� ��� ����� ���� ����������� ���� ���� ���������� ����\n������������ ������ ����������������������� ����������������������� ������� ��� ������ �����\n���������������\n��\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����� �������� ��� ���� ������ ���������� ������ �������� ��������� ������� ����������� ������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������� �����\n��\n�����\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_343": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 343 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 24TH MARCH, 2023 \n \n \nAYUSHMAN BHARAT YOJANA FOR HEALTH CARE SERVICES \n \n†*343. SHRI RAHUL KASWAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:                      \n \n(a) whether the Government has issued digital cards under the Ayushman Bharat \nYojana for providing healthcare services to the citizens in the country and if so, the \ndetails thereof, State/ UT-wise;  \n \n(b) whether the said digital cards are not being issued in many States/UTs where \nChiranjeevi Health Insurance Scheme and other similar schemes are rolled out by \nState Government and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has any Scheme for the patients in such States to cover \ntheir healthcare needs and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(d) whether the Government has conducted a survey of incurable diseases like heart \nattack and cancer prevalent in the country and if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise \nparticularly in Churu district of Rajasthan; and  \n \n(e) whether the Government proposes to implement Scheme for incurable diseases in \nthe country and if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE  \n(DR MANSUKH MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to ( e) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 343 FOR 24 TH MARCH, 2023 \n \n(a) to (e) Ayushman Bharat - Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) is the \nlargest publicly funded health protection scheme in the world which provides health \ncover of Rs. 5 lakh per family per year for secondary and tertiary care hospitalization \nto 60 crore beneficiaries. Many States/UTs implemen ting AB -PMJAY have \nexpanded the beneficiary base to approximately 15.5 crore families at their own cost.  \nIt is an entitlement -based scheme. No enrolment or registration of beneficiary is \nrequired to avail benefits under the scheme. The verified beneficiaries are issued PVC \nAyushman card under the scheme. The digital copy of the Ayushman card is shared \ninstantly once the request for Ayushman card is approved. Beneficiaries can also \ndownload their Ayushman Card. A total of 23.3 crore Ayushman cards have been \ncreated under the scheme, State/UT-wise details of which, are at Annexure. \n \nThe scheme is implemented in 33 States/UTs in convergence with over 20 \nState specific schemes. Co -branded Ayushman card is issued to the eligible \nbeneficiaries supported by Centre and State in all the 33 States/UTs. In Rajasthan, \nAB-PMJAY is implemented in convergence with the States’ health insurance scheme \nMukhyamantri Chiranjeevi Swasthya Yojana and the beneficiaries under the \nconverged scheme are also issued co-branded PVC Ayushman card. \n \nUnder Ayushman Bharat –Health and Wellness Centres (AB -HWCs), \ncomprehensive need -based healthcare services covering maternal and child health \nservices and non -communicable diseases, including free essential drugs and \ndiagnostic services are provided free of cost to all citizens of the country. \n \nAB-PMJAY provides treatment corresponding to a total of 1,949 procedures \nunder 27 different specialties including chronic diseases such as Cancer, Diabetes, \nHeart Disease and other incurable diseases. Of t hese, a total of 549 procedures are \nrelated to Cancer healthcare, while a total of 184 procedures are related to Cardiology \nand Cardiovascular and Thoracic Surgery. \nGovernment of India provides technical and financial support to the State/UTs \nunder the Nat ional Programme for Prevention and Control of Cancer, Diabetes, \nCardiovascular Diseases and Stroke (NPCDCS), as part of National Health Mission \n(NHM). The programme focusses on strengthening infrastructure, human resource \ndevelopment, health promotion & aw areness generation for Cancer prevention, early \ndiagnosis, management and referral to an appropriate level of healthcare facility for \ntreatment of the Non-Communicable Diseases (NCDs). Under NPCDCS, 708 District \nNCD Clinics, 301 District Day Care Centres, and 5671 Community Health Center \nNCD Clinics have been set up. \n\n \n \nGovernment of India implements \"Strengthening of Tertiary Care Cancer \nFacilities Scheme\" under NPCDCS to assist States/UTs in setting up of State Cancer \nInstitutes (SCIs) and Tertiary Care Cancer Centres (TCCCs) in different parts of the \ncountry in order t o enhance the facilities for tertiary care of cancer. 19 State Cancer \nInstitutes (SCIs) and 20 Tertiary Care Cancer Centres (TCCCs) have been approved \nunder the said scheme. 15 Institutes are functional so far. National Cancer Institute at \nJhajjar (Haryana ) and second campus of Chittaranjan National Cancer Institute, \nKolkata have also been set up. All existing and new AIIMS and many upgraded \ninstitutions under Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana (PMSSY) also focus on \ntreatment of Non-Communicable Diseases including cancer. \n  \n\n \n \n \n \nAnnexure \n \nState/UT-wise details of Ayushman cards created under the scheme \n \nState/UT Ayushman cards created \nAndaman And Nicobar Islands                               40,616  \nAndhra Pradesh                        11,709,939  \nArunachal Pradesh                               82,607  \nAssam                           7,502,411  \nBihar                           7,768,696  \nChandigarh                             141,662  \nChhattisgarh                        17,041,356  \nDadra and Nagar Haveli & Daman and Diu                             430,863  \nGoa                                27,076  \nGujarat                         17,743,275  \nHaryana                           8,137,302  \nHimachal Pradesh                          1,131,516  \nJammu And Kashmir                          8,142,855  \nJharkhand                        10,582,316  \nKarnataka                        13,697,728  \nKerala                           7,146,371  \nLadakh                              130,420  \nLakshadweep                               26,031  \nMadhya Pradesh                        35,534,316  \nMaharashtra                          9,161,278  \nManipur                              482,457  \nMeghalaya                          1,779,340  \nMizoram                              434,506  \nNagaland                             435,497  \nPuducherry                             409,804  \nPunjab                           7,990,610  \nRajasthan                        10,091,251  \nSikkim                                52,614  \nTamil Nadu                          2,786,818  \nTelangana                          4,198,258  \nTripura                           1,313,815  \nUttar Pradesh                        26,156,403  \nUttarakhand                          5,017,750  \n \nNote: Additional 1.6 crore beneficiaries have been verified using States’ IT system. \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_344": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AYURVEDA, YOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI, \nSIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY (AYUSH) \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 344 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 24TH MARCH, 2023 \n \n \n \nMEASURES TO IMPROVE AYUSH INFRASTRUCTURE \n \n†*344. SHRI RAJAN VICHARE:  \n  SHRI ARUN SAO:  \n \nWill the Minister of AYUSH be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken or proposes to take any measures to improve \nthe infrastructure of AYUSH services and accessibility thereof in various States;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor, State/UT -wise including \nMaharashtra, Chhattisgarh, Uttar Pradesh and Karnataka;  \n \n(c) the steps taken under the National AYUSH Mission (NAM) to promote the \ndevelopment of AYUSH system and med icines during the last three years, State/UT -\nwise; and  \n \n(d) the details of funds sanctioned, allocated and utilized under NAM during the last \nthree years, State/ UT-wise? \n \n \n \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF AYURVEDA, YOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI,  \nSIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY(AYUSH) \n \n  \n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL) \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 344* FOR 24TH MARCH, 2023 \n \n(a) to (d) Public Health being a State subject, the primary responsibility to improve \nthe infrastructure and increase access to AYUSH services in various States including \nMaharashtra, Chhattisgarh, Uttar Pradesh and Karnataka lies with the respective State \nGovernment. However, the Government of India has launched the Centrally \nSponsored Scheme of the National AYUSH Mission (NAM) implementing through \nStates/UTs including Maharashtra, Chhattisgarh, Uttar Pradesh and Karnataka for the \noverall development of AY USH systems also, including infrastructural development \nand access to AYUSH Services. National AYUSH Mission inter -alia makes \nprovisions for the following to promote the development of AYUSH systems and \nmedicines in the country including Maharashtra, Chhat tisgarh, Uttar Pradesh and  \nKarnataka:- \n(i) AYUSH Health & Wellness Centres (AHWCs) \n(ii) Co-location of AYUSH facilities at Primary Health Centres (PHCs), Community \nHealth Centres (CHCs) and District Hospitals (DHs)  \n(iii) Upgradation of existing standalone Government AYUSH Hospitals \n(iv) Upgradation of existing Government/Panchayat/Government aided AYUSH \nDispensaries/Construction of building for existing AYUSH Dispensary \n(Rented/dilapidated accommodation)/Construction of building to establish new \nAYUSH Dispensary \n(v) Setting up of up to 50/30/10 bedded integrated AYUSH Hospitals  \n(vi) Supply of essential drugs to Government AYUSH Hospitals, Government \nDispensaries and Government/Government aided Teaching Institutional AYUSH \nHospitals  \n(vii) AYUSH Public Health Programmes \n(viii) Infrastructural development of AYUSH Under -Graduate Institutions and AYUSH \nPost-Graduate Institutions  \n(ix) Establishment of new AYUSH Colleges in the States where availability of \nAYUSH teaching institutions is inadequate in the Government Sector. \n \nUnder NAM, the status of funds sanctioned/released as central share to various \nStates / UTs during the last three years and expenditure reported by them is furnished \nat Annexure.  \n \n\n \n \nAnnexure \nStatus of fund released as Central Share & expenditure reported by State / UT Governments \nunder National AYUSH Mission (NAM) during the last three years from 2019-20 to 2021-22 \n(Rs. in Lakhs) \nSl. \nNo. Name of States/UTs \n2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \nCentral \nShare \nreleased  \nExpenditure \nreported by \nState / UT \nCentral \nShare \nreleased  \nExpenditure \nreported by \nState / UT  \nCentral \nShare \nreleased  \nExpenditure \nreported by \nState / UT \n1 Andaman & Nicobar \nIslands 365.418 365.418 251.808 245.2765 296.0605 291.0605 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 1900.594 23.517 385.402 7.961 0 0 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 383.330 368.715 678.090 419.503 180.8500 0 \n4 Assam 1601.322 960.189 347.150 228.62 639.5200 366.02 \n5 Bihar 2661.298 85.874 516.535 32.36 1686.0770 0 \n6 Chandigarh 0.000 0 195.808 70.39 94.8640 0 \n7 Chhattisgarh 0 0 2691.066 1101.53 841.3090 231.79 \n8 Dadra & Nagar Haveli \nand Daman & Diu 63.854 33.455 0 0 0 0 \n9 Delhi 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n10 Goa 118.651 110.136 65.988 38.277 218.9880 0 \n11 Gujarat 2229.691 1,779.160 244.011 189.0900 466.9260 111.3600 \n12 Haryana 2299.475 2291.41 3034.422 2976.972 647.7020 552.634 \n13 Himachal Pradesh 2045.892 1548.203 494.940 400.223 1261.800 531 \n14 Jammu & Kashmir 1848.539 1747.227 2285.751 2143.1998 1313.105 1143.3548 \n15 Jharkhand 1522.312 1390.913 0.000 0 1309.765 1059.758 \n16 Karnataka 1791.709 1639.941 2184.371 1894.431 1821.460 1283.262 \n17 Kerala 1540.535 1451.5777 2337.588 2246.445 1153.388 1153.388 \n18 Ladakh 0 0 0 0 187.4500 25.12 \n19 Lakshadweep 426.878 415.086 19.605 18.009 64.2570 45.216 \n20 Madhya Pradesh 4012.347 3745.04 5608.633 5142.49 3123.1980 2575.189 \n21 Maharashtra 4308.643 2429.468 0 0 0 0 \n22 Manipur 907.075 645.165 571.720 274.706 170.0400 48.826 \n23 Mizoram 199.51 199.51 657.730 606.171 259.0800 227.67 \n24 Meghalaya 348.21 312.942 247.970 79.194 609.7800 333.341 \n25 Nagaland 950.58 950.58 1254.890 811.3975 232.2700 151.746 \n26 Odisha 726.096 352.8 716.640 468.85 1075.380 476.88 \n27 Puducherry 238.416 212.067 47.667 46.613 200.2730 188.96 \n28 Punjab 1155.493 14.103 89.770 0 527.2800 0 \n29 Rajasthan 1987.595 1228.62 2276.400 1246.388 3189.0000 45.504 \n30 Sikkim 330.593 330.593 350.440 350.44 99.3000 99.3 \n31 Tamil Nadu 1993.913 1993.913 616.580 484.211 2348.2680 1822.242 \n32 Telangana 934.178 687.121 0.000 0 3132.2520 2530.512 \n33 Tripura 0 0 270.080 133.74 138.7100 138.71 \n34 Uttar Pradesh 7923.69 7688.082 10373.858 9649.9671 13809.7240 11764.91 \n35 Uttarakhand 825.34 721.827 656.458 508.66 2622.5040 1417.99 \n\n36 West Bengal 1849.740 1236.832 247.3