    "ls|LS17_S11_U_361": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-361\nANSWERED ON- 03/02/2023\nPASSPORT OFFICE IN GONDIA\n†361. SHRI SUNIL BABURAO MENDHE\nWill the Minister of  EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state :-\n(a) whether the Government proposes to open a passport office in Gondia;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) if not, the reasons therefor?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n(SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN)\n(a to c) Ministry in association with Department of Posts (DOP) had announced in the year\n2017 opening of Passport Kendras at the Head Post Offices (HPO)/ Post Offices (PO) in the\ncountry called Post Office Passport Seva Kendra (POPSK) in each Lok Sabha Constituency\nwhere there is no Passport Seva Kendra (PSK) or a POPSK.  Under the above mentioned\npolicy, a POPSK at Bhandara is functional at Bhandara-Gondiya Lok Sabha Constituency. \n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_362": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF ECONOMIC AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *362 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, MARCH 27, 2023 /Chaitra 6, 1945 (Saka) \n \nFOREIGN INVESTMENTS FROM NEIGHBOURING COUNTRIES \n \n*362, SHRI N. REDDEPPA: \n \n Will the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has eased/proposes to ease restrictions on foreign \ninvestments from the companies that are based in countries that share land border with \nIndia or have an investor from these nations;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has any pending investment proposals from China and \nHong Kong awaiting Government clearance during the past year and the current year; \nand \n \n (d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nFINANCE MINISTER \n \n(SMT. NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n\n \n  STATEMENT REFFERED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 362 RAISED BY ������������������������������������������������������������������OF PARLIAMENT TO \nBE ANSWERED ON 27.03.2023 REGARDING FOREIGN INVESTMENT FROM \nNEIGHBOURING COUNTRIES \n \n(a) & (b) In order to curb opportunistic takeovers/acquisitions of Indian companies due \nto the COVID -19 pandemic, vide Press Note 3(2020) dated 17.04.2020, Go vernment \namended the FDI policy according to which an entity of a country, which shares land \nborder with India or where the beneficial owner of an investment into India is situated in \nor is a citizen of any such country, can invest only under the Governmen t route. \nAdditionally, any transfer of ownership of any existing or future FDI in an entity in India \nresulting in the beneficial ownership falling within the aforesaid jurisdiction(s) will also \nrequire Government approval.  \n \nNo such proposal is under consideration of the Government. \n \n(c) & (d). Yes Sir, 54 FDI Proposals received during the past year and current year with \ninvestor/ beneficial owner from China/Hong Kong are pending for decision  with \nGovernment as on 21.03.2023. \n \n**** ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_363": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 363 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 27.03.2023 \n \nENROLMENT UNDER PM-SYM SCHEME \n \n*363. SHRIMATI GODDETI MADHAVI: \n \n Will the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)whether it is true that the enrolment drive under the Pradhan \nMantri Shram Yogi Maan -Dhan (PM -SYM) Scheme was adversely \naffected due to the COVID-19 pandemic and resultant lockdowns; \n(b)if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by the Government \nto in crease the enrolment in the aftermath of the COVID -19 \npandemic; \n(c)whether the Government is undertaking periodic inspections and \naudits of the implementing agencies under the PM -SYM scheme; \nand \n(d)if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BHUPENDER YADAV) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*                                                   ****** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED  TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (d ) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *363 TO BE ANSWERED ON \n27.03.2023 RAISED BY  SHRIMATI GODDETI MADHAVI  REGARDING \nENROLMENT UNDER PM-SYM SCHEME. \n \n(a) to (d): The enrolment count in the Pradhan Mantri Shram Yogi \nMaan-Dhan (PM-SYM) Scheme in the year 2018-19 was 27.43 lakh, in \nthe year  2019 -20 was 16.11 lakh, in the year  2020 -21 was 1.72 \nlakh, in the year 2021 -22 was 1.28 lakh and in the year 2022 -23 it \nwas 2.71 lakhs. The total enrolment in the scheme as on date is \napproximately 49.28 lakhs. \nTo increase the enrolment in the PMSYM government has \norganised mega enrolment camps. Further, to make the scheme \nmore attractive, Donate -a-Pension Module was launched.  Besides, \nthe Ministry is holding periodic review meeting with Labour \nDepartment officers of States/UTs District Administration.  Review \nmeetings are convened from time to time with Common Service \nCenters (CSCs) State heads and LIC to encourage them to mobilize \nthe eligible beneficiaries. Extensive social media campaign has \nbeen launched thr ough social media handles of the Ministry. Funds \nwere released to States/ UTs to  undertake Information, Education \nand Communication (IEC) activities to mobilize the workers and to \nencourage them to register under this scheme. IEC materials such \nas Pamphlet s, Backdrops, creatives for standee and Video \ndocumentaries (in local language) was also sent to States.  \nLife Insurance Corporation of India (LIC) has conducted \nConfiguration Audit and Vulnerability Assessment (CA VA) Audit on \n12.12.2022.  LIC internal Au dit / Inspection departments are also \nperiodically reviewing the working of the Scheme. \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_364": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AYUSH \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 364  \nTO BE ANSWERED FOR 03.02.2023 \n \nPPP PROJECTS IN AYUSH SECTOR \n364.  SHRI ADALA PRABHAKARA REDDY: \n         SHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR BELLANA: \nWill the Minister of AYUSH be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has taken any steps to increase Public Private Partnership (PPP) \nprojects in the AYUSH sector; \n(b) if so, the details thereof including the number of such projects implemented and those in \nthe pipeline;  \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor;  \n(d) whether the Government has taken any steps to attract private investment in the AYUSH \nsector; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF AYUSH \n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL) \n(a) to (c): \nYes,  \ni. Ministry of Ayush implements a Central Sector Scheme namely Champion Services \nSector Scheme for Medical Value Travel with a total financial outlay of Rs. 769 \nCrores. There are three components of this scheme i.e. (1) Establishment of Ayush \nSuper speciality Hospitals / Daycare Centres  (2) Skill development in Ayush sector \nand (3) Establishment of Ayush Grid. Under Establishment of Ayush Super speciality \nHospitals / Daycare Centres  financial assistance in the form of interest subsidy  \nmaximum upto Rs. 8.15 Crores is provided to the private investors for Establishment \nof World Class, State of the Art Super Specialty Hospitals/ Day Care Centres of the \nsystems recognized under Indian Medicine Central Council (IMCC) Act, 1970 or \nHomeopathic Central Council (HCC)  Act, 1973 on Pan India basis.  Total financial \noutlay of this component is Rs. 514 Crores. \n\nii. Ministry of Ayush implements AYURSWASTHYA Yojana comprising 03 \ncomponents i.e. (1) Ayush & Public Health (2) A yush for sports medicine and (3) \nUpgradation of facilit ies to Centre of Excellence (CoE).  This scheme has been \napproved for F.Y. 2021 -22 to 2025 -26 with financial outlay Rs.11 Crore for every \nfinancial year.  Under the Centre of Excellence component of AYURSWASTHYA \nYojana, financial assistance of maximum Rs. 1 0 crores  is provided to eligible \nindividual organizations/institutes for establishing and upgrading their functions & \nfacilities and/or for research & development activities in Ayush. The objectives of the \nCentre of Excellence component of AYURSWASTHYA Yojana are as under: - \na. To support establishment of advanced/ specialized Ayush medical health unit in \nreputed Ayush and Allopathic institutions both in Government and Non -Government \nsector. \nb. To support creative and innovative proposals for establishment and up gradation of \nboth functions and facilities of reputed institutions to strengthen competencies of \nAyush professionals in education technology, research & innovation and such other \nfields necessary for promotion of Ayush at national as well as international level. \nc. To support creative and innovative proposals for prestigious organizations which have \nwell-established buildings and infrastructure, and wish to work for Ayush systems to \nthe level of Centre of Excellence. \niii. Ministry of Ayush is implementing Central S ector Scheme for Ayush Oushadhi \nGunavatta evam Uttpadan Samvardhan Yojana (AOGUSY)  for the year 2021 -2026 \nwith financial outlay of Rs. 122 Crore with the following  Components- \na. Strengthening and up -gradation of Ayush Pharmacies and Drug Testing Laboratories \nto achieve higher standards. \nb. Pharmacovigilance of ASU&H drugs including surveillance of misleading \nadvertisements.  \nc. Strengthening of Central and State regulatory frameworks including Technical \nHuman Resource & Capacity Building programs for Ayush drugs.  \nd. Support for development of standards and accreditation/certification of Ayush \nproducts & materials in collaboration with Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS), Quality \nControl of India (QCI) and other relevant scientific  institutions and industrial R&D \ncentres.  \nThe objectives of the scheme are as under:- \n1. To enhance India's manufacturing capabilities and exports of traditional medicines and \nhealth promotion products under the initiative of Atmanirbhar Bharat.  \n2. To facilitate adequate infrastructural & technological up gradation and institutional \nactivities in public and private sector for standardization, quality manufacturing and \nanalytical testing of Ayush drugs & materials. \n\n3. To strengthen regulatory frameworks at Central and State level for effective quality \ncontrol, safety monitoring and surveillance of misleading advertisements of Ayush \ndrugs. \n4. To encourage building up synergies, collaborations and convergent approaches for \npromoting standards and quality of Ayush drugs & materials. \n(d) & (e): \nYes, \ni. Ministry of Ayush has signed a MoU with Invest India for establishment of Strategic Policy \nand Facilitation Bureau (SPFB) in respect of Ministry of Ayush. The objective of SPFB \nincludes Strategic and Policy - Making s upport, State policy Bench marking providing \nstrategic inputs to identify new potential domestic and foreign markets in the Ayush sector \nand Knowledge creation and management including inputs and support on policy matters, \nresearch etc.  \nii. Ministry of Ayush in collaboration with Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) and Institute \nof Teaching and Research in Ayurveda, Jamnagar organised a Global Ayush Investment and \nInnovation Summit (GAIIS), 2022 with an objective to bring together country’s key startups, \nentrepreneurs, investors, policy makers and other national/international stakeholders for a \nspecially curated event on innovation and make India a Global Ayush destination for \nentrepreneurship. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_365": "������������������� �\n������������������������������������� �\n��������������������������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n�������������������������� �\n������������������� �� ��������������� �\n�\n������������������������� �\n�\n����� ������������������ �\n�\n���������������������������� ������������������ ����������������������\n�\n���� �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������\n�������� ������� ��� ����������� ���� �������� ��������������� ������� ������� ������������ ����\n�����������������������������������������������\n���� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������\n�\n� ����� �\n���������������������������������������������������� �\n�������������� �\n�������������������������� �\n�\n���� �� ���� ���� ����� ���������� ������� ��� ����������� ���� �������� �������������� ���� �������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������� ������� ��������� ���� ���������� ��������� �������� ������� ������� �������������� �����\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������� ���������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������\n�\n\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������� ��������� ������������������ ���� ����������� ����������� ��������� ������� ���\n������� �������� ���������� ���� ������� ������� ������� ��� ������ �������� ������� �������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ ���������� �������� � ���������\n�������� �������� �������� �������� �������� ��������\n��� ������� � ������� ������ ������� ������ ������ �����\n��� ������� � ������� ������ ������ ����� ����� �����\n��� ���� ������ ������ ������ ����� ����� �����\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������\n�\n�\n�\n�����\n� �\n\n�������� ���\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������\n�\n������� ��������\n���������\n�������������� ��������������\n������������\n��������������\n������ �\n������ ����� ������ ����� ������ �����\n�� ������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� ������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� �������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� �������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� ����� � �� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� ������������ ��� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� ������ � �� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� �������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n�� ����� � �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ����� � �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ����������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� �������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ������� � �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� �������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ���������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ������ �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ������� � �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ������� ��� ��� ���\n������������ �� ��� ��\n��� ���������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ���������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� �������� �� �� �� �� �� ��\n��� ����������� � �� �� �� �� �� ��\n� ������ ��� ��� ��� �� ��� ��\n�\n�\n�\n\n���������������\n�\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������\n�\n������� ����������������� �������� �������� ��������\n�� ������� ����� ����� �����\n�� ������� ���� ���� ����\n�� �������� ���� ���� ����\n�� �������� ����� ����� �����\n�� ����� � ����� ����� �����\n�� ������������ ������ ������ ������\n�� ������ � ���� ���� ����\n�� �������� ���� ���� ����\n�� ����� � ���� ���� ����\n��� ����� � ����� ����� �����\n��� ����������� ����� ����� �����\n��� �������� ���� ���� ����\n��� ������� ���� ����� �����\n��� ������� � ���� ���� ����\n��� �������� ���� ���� ����\n��� ���������� ���� ����� �����\n��� ������ ���� ���� ����\n��� ������� ������ ������ ������\n��� ������� � ����� ����� �����\n��� ������� ������ ������ ������\n��� ���������� ���� ���� ����\n��� ���������� ���� ����� �����\n��� �������� ���� ���� ����\n��� ����������� � ���� ���� ����\n� ������ ������ ������ ������\n�\n�\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_366": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *366 \nANSWERED ON 27.03.2023 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT IN JHARKHAND \n \n*366. SHRI JAYANT SINHA: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of various skill development centres in Hazaribagh and Ramgarh districts \nin Jharkhand; \n(b) the number of candidates who have completed training in these centres; and \n(c) the details of upcoming and ongoing initiatives of the Government in Hazaribagh \nand Ramgarh districts in Jharkhand? \n \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (c)  A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *366 TO BE ANSWERED ON 27.03.2023 ASKED BY SHRI \nJAYANT SINHA REGARDING SKILL DEVELOPMENT IN JHARKHAND \n \n(a) to (c) Under Skill India Mission, Ministry of Skill Development and \nEntrepreneurship (MSDE) delivers skill training to all the sections of the society. Training \nis imparted through a comprehensive network of skill development centres/ institutes \nacross the country including in the Hazaribagh and Ramgarh Districts of Jharkhand, under \nvarious ongoing schemes viz. Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY), Jan \nShikshan Sansthan (JSS), National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS) and \nCraftsmen Training Scheme (CTS) through Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs). The number \nof such training centres/ institutes and number of persons trained in Hazaribagh and \nRamgarh districts of Jharkhand are given in the table below. \n \nScheme Hazaribagh Ramgarh \n \nNumber of Training Centres/Institutes \nPMKVY 14 9 \nJSS 1 1 \nNAPS (No. of Establishments) 32 29 \nITIs 20 8 \n \nNumber of Persons Trained \nPMKVY (since 2015-16 to 31.12.2022) 25,917 15,401 \nJSS (Since 2018-19 to 31.12.2022) 7,239 1,495 \nNAPS (2018-19 to 31.12.2022) 807 1,537 \nITI  (2018-19 to 2021-22) 7,835 2,925 \n \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_367": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-367\nANSWERED ON-03/02/2023\nG-20 LEADERS SUMMIT\n367. SHRI P. RAVINDHRANATH \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state :-\n(a) whether the Government proposes to discuss about peace, harmony, stability and security \nof Indian Fishermen in “Indo-Pacific Region”, during the “G-20 Leaders Summit”, scheduled\nin the month of September 2023 at New Delhi;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) the details of the meetings under G-20 summit proposed/likely to be held in Tamil Nadu; \nand\n(d) the manner in which the Government proposes to utilize this opportunity for the benefit of\nthe country?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN)\n(a  &  b)  The  Group  of  Twenty  (G20)  is  the  premier  forum  for  international  economic\ncooperation. It plays an important role in shaping and strengthening global architecture and\ngovernance on major international economic issues. Some of the substantive deliberations in\nbroad priority areas during our G20 Presidency are inter alia revolving around inclusive and\nresilient  growth;  progress  on  Sustainable  Development  Goals;  green  development  and\nLifestyle for Environment (Mission LiFE); technological transformation and public digital\ninfrastructure; reforming multilateral institutions; women led development; and international\npeace and harmony.\n(c & d) During its G20 Presidency, India will host around 200 meetings in over 30 different\nworkstreams, comprising of Sherpa Track Working Groups, Finance Track workstreams,\nMinisterial Meetings and Engagement Groups. These would be held across the country,\nincluding in Tamil Nadu. The G20 Leaders’ Summit has been scheduled for 9-10 September\n2023 in New Delhi. The exact dates and venues are periodically updated on G20 website. \n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_368": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 368 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03rd February, 2023 \nSAINIK SCHOOLS \n368. SHRI ANNASAHEB SHANKAR JOLLE:  \nSHRI JASWANT SINGH BHABHOR: \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE be pleased to state: \n(a)  the number of Sainik Schools established since 2016, year-wise and State/UT-wise; \n(b)  the reason for not opening any new Sainik School in Karnataka; \n(c)  whether any communication has been sent tothe Government of Karnataka regarding \nopening of the Sainik School in the State; and \n(d)  if so, the details thereof alongwith the response received in this regard? \nA  N  S  W  E  R \n \n      MINISTER OF STATE     (SHRI AJAY BHATT) \n      IN THE MINISTRY OF DEFENCE \n \n(a):  A total of 08 Sainik Schools have been established since 2016 on erstwhile pattern. \nThe details of these schools year-wise and State/UT-wise is at Annexure-A. Under the \nnew initiative of setting up of 100 New Sainik Schools in partnership mode with \nPrivate/NGOs/State Governments, Sainik Schools Society have signed Memorandum \nof Agreement with 18 New Sainik Schools. The details of these New Sainik Schools is \nat Annexure-B. \n(b) to (d):  Two Sainik Schools namely Sainik School Bijapur and Sainik School \nKodagu under erstwhile pattern of Sainik Schools are already functioning in the State \nof Karnataka. Further, under the new initiative of setting up of 100 New Sainik Schools \nin partnership mode with NGOs/Private/State Government Schools, two new Sainik \nSchools have been opened in the State of Karnataka namely Sangolli Rayanna Sainik \nSchool, Belagavi and Viveka School of Excellence, Mysuru. \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE-A REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 368 TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2023 \nREGARDING “SAINIK SCHOOLS”. \n \nSainik Schools opened since 2016 on erstwhile pattern. \n***** \n�� ��\nS. No. Year State Name of School \n1.  2017 Mizoram Sainik School Chhingchhip \n2.  2018 Rajasthan Sainik School Jhunjhunu \n3.  2018 Arunachal Pradesh Sainik School East Siang \n4.  2019 Maharashtra Sainik School Chandrapur \n5.  2019  \nUttar Pradesh \n \nSainik School Jhansi \n6.  2019 Sainik School Mainpuri \n7.  2020 Sainik School Amethi \n8.  2020 Odisha  Sainik School Sambalpur  \n\nANNEXURE-B REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 368 TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2023 \nREGARDING “SAINIK SCHOOLS”. \nDETAILS OF 18 NEW SAINIK SCHOOLS (IN PARTNERSHIP MODE)  \n \nS.No State/UT Number of approved New Sainik Schools \nwith whom Sainik Schools Society signed  \nMemorandum of Agreement \n1 Maharashtra 2 \n2 Karnataka 2 \n3 Himachal Pradesh 1 \n4 Gujarat 2 \n5 Haryana 2 \n6 Bihar 2 \n7 Andhra Pradesh 1 \n8 Punjab 1 \n9 Arunachal Pradesh 1 \n10 Kerala 1 \n11 Tamil Nadu 1 \n12 Madhya Pradesh 1 \n13 Dadra and Nagar Haveli 1 \n��\n������������",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_369": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION  \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 369 \nANSWERED ON 27TH MARCH, 2023 \n \nPlacement of Students availing Scholarship for Higher Education \n*369 SHRIMATI PRATIMA MONDAL:  \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n(a)    Whether there is any provision for ensuring placement of students after completion of \nhigher education under various schemes providing scholarships to students; \n(b)    if so, the details thereof; and \n(c)    the details of scholarship provided by foreign institution to Indian students? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \n(a) to (c):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (C) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 369 ANSWERED ON 27.03.2023 ASKED BY HON’BLE \nM.P. SHRIMATI PRATIMA MONDAL REGARDING ‘PLACEMENT OF \nSTUDENTS AVAILING SCHOLARSHIP FOR HIGHER EDUCATION’. \n \n(a) to (b): The Government is implementing various scholarship schemes with t he objective  \nto provide financial assistance to meritorious and economically weaker students  to complete \ntheir higher education. The scholarship schemes are implemented online as per the respective \nscheme guidelines through the National Scholarships Portal (NSP) namely \nhttps://scholarships.gov.in. The scholarships are for higher education and placement is not a \npart of the scheme. \n \n(c): Under  the Cultural and Educational exchange programme, friendly foreign countries \nnamely, Hungary, Italy, South Korea, New Zealand, United Kingdom etc. are offering \nscholarships to Indian students for pursuing Higher Education in these countries.  \n**** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_370": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 370 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 27.03.2023 \n \nMIGRATION FOR EMPLOYMENT \n \n†*370. SHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL:  \n   SHRI RAMCHARAN BOHRA:  \n \n   Will the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n \n(a)whether the Government has taken a joint initiative with the State \nGovernments to control the migration for employment and if so, the \ndetails thereof, State-wise particularly of Bundelkhand;  \n(b)the details of the efforts being made for employment generation in \nBundelkhand; \n(c)whether the Government is aware of the migration of \nlabourers/unemployed youth from rural areas of the country, if so, \nthe details thereof along with the reasons therefor;  \n(d)the number of labourers migrated during each of the last three \nyears and the current year, State-wise/UT-wise; and \n(e)the remedial measures taken/being taken by the Government to \nprevent the migration of labourers/ unemployed youths and to \nprovide work to them near their place of residence? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BHUPENDER YADAV) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*                                                   ****** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (e) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 370* FOR REPLY ON 27/03/2023 \nRAISED BY SHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL & SHRI \nRAMCHARAN BOHRA REGARDING MIGRATION FOR EMPLOYMENT. \n \n(a) to (e): The Central Government in coordination with  State \nGovernments is implementing various developmental schemes for \ncreating employment opportunities and improving rural infrastructure \nto encourage people to stay in rural areas, earn their livelihood and \nraise their quality of life near their places of  residence and hence act \nas a deterrent to distress migration of rural population. Some of such \nschemes being implemented including in Bundelkhand are: \n \nMahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee \nScheme (MGNREGS), provides for guaranteed wage employment of 100 \ndays in a financial year to a rural household whose adult members are \nwilling to take up manual work. Further, an additional 50 days of wage \nemployment is provided over and above 100 days in the notified \ndrought affected areas or natural calam ity affected areas in the \ncountry. \nDeendayal Antyodaya Yojana  – National Rural Livelihoods \nMission (DAY -NRLM) is implemented with the objective of providing \nself-employment to the women members of the rural poor families by \nmobilizing them into Self Help Groups (SHGs). \n \nRural Self Employment and Training Institutes (RSETIs) \nprovides for skill development programme for self -employment. This \ntraining with access to Bank loans helps in creating self -employment \nopportunities at local level. \n \nShyama Prasad Mukherji Rurban Mission (SPMRM) is aimed \nat developing 300 rural g rowth clusters called ‘Rurban Clusters’ which \nhave latent potential for growth, in all States and UTs. These clusters \nwere conceptualized with the objective to bridge the rural -urban \ndivide, reduce migration from rural to urban areas and eventually \nfacilitate reverse migration. \n     \nPradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana (PMMY) was launched by the \nGovernment for facilitating self -employment. Under PMMY, collateral \nfree loans upto Rs. 10 lakh, are extended to micro/small business \nenterprises and to individuals to enabl e them to setup or expand their \nbusiness activities.  \n\nThe Production Linked Incentive (PLI) scheme is being \nimplemented by the Government with an outlay of Rs. 1.97 lakh crore, \nfor a period of 5 years starting from 2021 -22 which have potential for \ncreating 60 lakh new jobs. \nPM GatiShakti is a transformative approach for economic \ngrowth and sustainable development. The approach is driven by seven \nengines, namely, Roads, Railways, Airports, Ports, Mass Transport, \nWaterways and Logistics Infrastructure. This a pproach is powered by \nClean Energy and Sabka Prayas leading to huge job and \nentrepreneurial opportunities for all. \n          Besides these initiatives, various flagship programmes of \nthe Government such as Make in India, Start -up India, Stand -up India, \nDigital India, Housing for All etc. are also oriented towards generating \nemployment opportunities in the country including the State of Uttar \nPradesh. All these initiatives are expected to collectively generate \nemployment in the medium to long term through multiplier-effects. \nAs per the Report Migration in India, 2020 -21, based on \nPLFS 2020 -21, released by Ministry of Statistics and Programme \nImplementation (MoSPI), the total migration rate in India was 28.9% \nand in rulal was 26.5%. Out of the total migrant persons, around 10.8% \npersons were migrated due to employment related reasons. The \nemployment related reasons include in search of employment/better \nemployment, for employment/ work (to take up employment/ to take up \nbetter employment/ business/ proximity to place of work/ transfer) and \nloss of job/closure of unit/lack of employment opportunities. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_371": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO-371 \nANSWERED ON- 27.03.2023 \n \nCLASSICAL STATUS TO INDIAN LANGUAGES \n \n \n*371. ADV. A.M. ARIFF: \n           \n Will the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the details of the Indian languages which  have been accorded the classical \nlanguage status; \n(b) whether the Government has implemented any schemes to provide financial  \nassistance to various projects of classical language; \n(c) if so, the details thereof; \n(d) the details of the funds provided for each  classical language during each of \nthe last three years, language-wise; \n(e) whether the Government has received any  proposal regarding the classical \nlanguage projects during the last three years; and \n(f) if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \n(a)  to (f) :     A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 371 TO BE ANSWERED ON 27.03.2023 ASKED \nBY ADV. A.M. ARIFF, HON’BLE M.P. REGARDING “ CLASSICAL STATUS TO \nINDIAN LANGUAGES” \n \n \n(a) to  (d): Six Indian languages namely Sanskrit, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, \nMalayalam and Odia have been accorded the status of Classical Language. The \npolicy of the Government is to promote all Indian languages including classical \nlanguages. Central Institute of Indian Languages (CIIL) works for the promotion \nof all Indian languages including four classical languages viz. Kannada, Telugu, \nMalayalam and Odia. Development and promotion of Classical Tamil is done by \nCentral Institute of Classical Tamil (CICT). The Government of India is promoting \nSanskrit Language through three Central Universities. Funds are provided to \nthese universities for teaching and research in Sanskrit Language leading  to \naward of degree, diploma, certificate to students and no separate funds are \nprovided for undertaking any work related to classical aspect of Sanskrit. The \ndetails of funds provided for various classical languages are given below: \n                                                                                             (Rs. in lakhs) \nLanguage 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \nKannada 107.00 108.00 106.50 \nTelugu 107.00 147.00 103.15 \nMalayalam Nil 8.00 63.97 \nTamil 770. 00 1200.00 1200.00 \nOdia Nil 8.00 58.38 \n \n(e) & (f): No other proposal has been received in respect of classical language \nprojects. \n \n****  \n ",
