\u0000W\u0000K\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000\u0003 \u0000\u0014\u0000\u0018\u0000\u0013\u0000\u0003\n\u0000P\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000X\u0000I\u0000D\u0000F\u0000W\u0000X\u0000U\u0000H\u0000U\u0000V\u0000\u0003\u0000R\u0000I\u0000\u0003\u0000H\u0000F\u0000R\u0000\u0010\u0000D\u0000O\u0000W\u0000H\u0000U\u0000Q\u0000D\u0000W\u0000L\u0000Y\u0000H\u0000V\u0000\u0003\u0000I\u0000U\u0000R\u0000P\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000F\u0000U\u0000R\u0000V\u0000V\u0000\u0003\u0000W\u0000K\u0000H\u0000\u0003\u0000F\u0000R\u0000X\u0000Q\u0000W\u0000U\u0000\\\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000U\u0000H\u0000\u0003\u0000S\u0000D\u0000U\u0000W\u0000L\u0000F\u0000L\u0000S\u0000D\u0000W\u0000L\u0000Q\u0000J\u0000\u0003\u0000L\u0000Q\u0000\u0003\u0000W\u0000K\u0000H\u0000\u0003\u0000(\u0000[\u0000S\u0000R\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0003\u00007\u0000K\u0000H\u0000\u0003\n\u0000(\u0000F\u0000R\u0000\u0010\u0000D\u0000O\u0000W\u0000H\u0000U\u0000Q\u0000D\u0000W\u0000L\u0000Y\u0000H\u0000V\u0000\u0003\u0000Z\u0000H\u0000U\u0000H\u0000\u0003\u0000P\u0000D\u0000G\u0000H\u0000\u0003\u0000I\u0000U\u0000R\u0000P\u0000\u0003\u0000F\u0000R\u0000L\u0000U\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0003\u0000E\u0000D\u0000J\u0000D\u0000V\u0000V\u0000H\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0003\u0000U\u0000L\u0000F\u0000H\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000G\u0000\u0003\u0000Z\u0000K\u0000H\u0000D\u0000W\u0000\u0003\u0000E\u0000U\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0003\u0000S\u0000O\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000W\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000G\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000J\u0000U\u0000L\u0000F\u0000X\u0000O\u0000W\u0000X\u0000U\u0000D\u0000O\u0000\u0003\n\u0000U\u0000H\u0000V\u0000L\u0000G\u0000X\u0000H\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0003\u0000E\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000D\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000G\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000U\u0000H\u0000F\u0000D\u0000\u0003\u0000O\u0000H\u0000D\u0000Y\u0000H\u0000V\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0003\u0000M\u0000X\u0000W\u0000H\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000G\u0000\u0003\u0000F\u0000O\u0000R\u0000W\u0000K\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0003\u0000$\u0000Z\u0000D\u0000U\u0000H\u0000Q\u0000H\u0000V\u0000V\u0000\u0003\u0000J\u0000H\u0000Q\u0000H\u0000U\u0000D\u0000W\u0000L\u0000R\u0000Q\u0000\u0003\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000G\u0000\u0003\u0000F\u0000D\u0000S\u0000D\u0000F\u0000L\u0000W\u0000\\\u0000\u0003\u0000E\u0000X\u0000L\u0000O\u0000G\u0000L\u0000Q\u0000J\u0000\u0003\n\u0000S\u0000U\u0000R\u0000J\u0000U\u0000D\u0000P\u0000P\u0000H\u0000V\u0000\u0003 \u0000K\u0000D\u0000Y\u0000H\u0000\u0003 \u0000E\u0000H\u0000H\u0000Q\u0000\u0003 \u0000R\u0000U\u0000J\u0000D\u0000Q\u0000L\u0000]\u0000H\u0000G\u0000\u0003 \u0000I\u0000R\u0000U\u0000\u0003 \u0000H\u0000O\u0000L\u0000P\u0000L\u0000Q\u0000D\u0000W\u0000L\u0000R\u0000Q\u0000\u0003 \u0000R\u0000I\u0000\u0003 \u0000V\u0000L\u0000Q\u0000J\u0000O\u0000H\u0000\u0003 \u0000X\u0000V\u0000H\u0000\u0003 \u0000S\u0000O\u0000D\u0000V\u0000W\u0000L\u0000F\u0000V\u0000\u0003 \u0000I\u0000R\u0000U\u0000\u0003 \u0000S\u0000O\u0000D\u0000V\u0000W\u0000L\u0000F\u0000\u0003 \u0000Z\u0000D\u0000V\u0000W\u0000H\u0000\u0003\n\u0000P\u0000L\u0000Q\u0000L\u0000P\u0000L\u0000]\u0000D\u0000W\u0000L\u0000R\u0000Q\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0003\n\u0000\u0003\n\u0000\r\u0000\r\u0000\r\u0000\u0003\n��\n��\n\u0000\u0003\n\u0000\u0003\n\u0000\u0003",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_444": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION\nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION No-444\nANSWERED ON 03/04/2023\nStatus of Girls Education in India\n*444. SHRIMATI SUMALATHA AMBAREESH:\nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has any data regarding the status of girls education in the\ncountry, if so, the details thereof, State-wise/district-wise including Karnataka;\n(b) whether the Government has any data regarding the higher education enrolment ratio of\ngirls in the country including Karnataka, if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) the approximate percentage of girls enrolled in higher education sector who find\nplacements and jobs in the country, State-wise?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF EDUCATION\n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN)\n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (A) TO (C) OF LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 444 ANSWERED ON 3rd APRIL, 2023 REGARDING\nSTATUS OF GIRLS EDUCATION IN INDIA ASKED BY SHRIMATI SUMALATHA\nAMBAREESH, HON’BLE MP:\n(a) & (b) Yes Sir. The Unified District Information System for Education Plus (UDISE+)\nand All India Survey on Higher Education (AISHE) are two of the sources for data\ncollection on School Education and Higher Education respectively. State-wise Enrolment of\nGirls in School Education and District wise Girls Enrolment in Karnataka is at Annexure I.\nState-wise Female Enrolment and Female Gross Enrolment Ratio (GER) in Higher\nEducation and District wise Female Enrolment (Higher Education) in Karnataka is at\nAnnexure II.\nAs per UDISE+, the total enrolment of girls in 2021-22 from primary to higher\nsecondary levels of school education is 12.28 Crore. The girls enrolment in higher\nsecondary has been increased to 1.4 crore in year 2021-22 from 1.2 crore in 2018-19.\nAs per latest AISHE 2020-21, the female enrolment has increased significantly to\n2.01 crore, from 1.57 crore in 2014-15, thus reflecting an 28% increase since 2014-15.\nSimilarly, there has been appreciable increase of 33.62% in the female enrolment in Higher\nEducation in Karnataka, to 12.17 Lakh in 2020-21 from 9.11 Lakh in 2014-15.\nA significant achievement for the country is that the Female Gross Enrolment Ratio\n(GER) in Higher Education, has overtaken the male GER since 2017-18. Further, the\nfemale GER has increased to 27.9 in 2020-21 from 22.9 in 2014-15. Remarkably, Female\nGER of Karnataka has increased to 37.2 in 2020-21 from 26.7 in 2014-15.\n(c) Education is a subject matter of Concurrent list and Educational Institutions are\nmanaged by both Central and State Governments. There are many private institutions also.\nMajority of the Educational Institutions in the country fall under the purview of the State /\nUT Government. Further, now students have multiple choices/options such as higher\nstudies, research, start-ups, entrepreneurship, etc. and as such placement is not a common\nfunction across all institutions. As such, data of placements and jobs of females students in\nHigher Education is distributed across Institutions and States/UTs.\nIn this regard, the University Grants Commission (UGC) has facilitated Higher\nEducational Institutions (HEIs) across the country to provide skill-based education under\nNational Skills Qualification Framework (NSQF) which impart vocational and employment\noriented education. In order to further improve employability of students including girls\nstudents, the UGC has introduced Apprenticeship Embedded Degree programme in the year\n2020. The UGC is also implementing two special scholarship / fellowship schemes for\nsingle girl child namely (1) ‘Post Graduate Indira Gandhi Scholarship for Single Girl Child’\n(2) ‘Savitribai Jyotirao Phule Fellowship for Single Girl Child’.\nSimilarly, All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE) has taken initiatives\nsuch as advising technical institutions enter into MoUs with atleast 5 industries for\nstrengthening academia-industry interaction, offering of elective courses in new emerging\nareas such as Data Science, AI, etc, and mandating of internship for engineering students,\netc., to improve the chances of placement for students, including women.\nFurther, in Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs) and National Institutes of\nTechnology (NITs), supernumerary seats have been created to enhance participation of\nwomen in these institutions, which makes more women job ready.\n******\n\nAnnexure-I\nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (A) & (B) OF LOK SABHA STARRED\nQUESTION NO. 444 ANSWERED ON 03.04.2023 ASKED BY HON’BLE MP SHRIMATI\nSUMALATHA AMBAREESH REGARDING STATUS OF GIRLS EDUCATION IN INDIA\nEnrolment of Girls Students in School Education (Pre-Primary to Higher Secondary), 2021-22\nStates/UT Girls\nAndaman and Nicobar Islands 36325\nAndhra Pradesh 3966632\nArunachal Pradesh 177046\nAssam 3824912\nBihar 13418639\nChandigarh 124916\nChhattisgarh 2978951\nD & N Haveli and Daman & Diu 63290\nDelhi 2160784\nGoa 147955\nGujarat 5383540\nHaryana 2729492\nHimachal Pradesh 684325\nJammu and Kashmir 1294730\nJharkhand 3909912\nKarnataka 5858267\nKerala 3150928\nLadakh 30125\nLakshadweep 6589\nMadhya Pradesh 7710880\nMaharashtra 10632059\nManipur 340995\nMeghalaya 597198\nMizoram 153688\nNagaland 221287\nOdisha 3696130\nPuducherry 124774\nPunjab 2828096\nRajasthan 8215519\nSikkim 67255\nTamil Nadu 6251956\nTelangana 3329550\nTripura 354547\nUttar Pradesh 22305757\nUttarakhand 1153720\nWest Bengal 9404483\nIndia 127335252\n\nDistrict-wise, Girls Enrolment in School Education (Pre-Primary to Higher Secondary)\nin Karnataka, 2021-22\nDistrict Girls\nBAGALKOT 213574\nBALLARI 146227\nBELAGAVI 215942\nBELAGAVI CHIKKODI 275425\nBENGALURU RURAL 89430\nBENGALURU U NORTH 394412\nBENGALURU U SOUTH 610492\nBIDAR 186029\nCHAMARAJANAGARA 69520\nCHIKKABALLAPURA 99901\nCHIKKAMANGALURU 82566\nCHITRADURGA 140363\nDAKSHINA KANNADA 193151\nDAVANAGERE 153022\nDHARWAD 191874\nGADA