    "ls|LS17_S11_U_455": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION\nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION AND LITERACY\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 455\nANSWERED ON 03.04.2023\nTeacher-Student Ratio and Basic Amenities in Government Schools\n*455. DR. KRISHNA PAL SINGH YADAV:\nPROF. RITA BAHUGUNA JOSHI:\nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:\n(a) the steps taken by the Government to improve the teacher-student ratio in\nGovernment schools;\n(b) the steps taken by the Government to improve the quality of teachers in\nGovernment schools;\n(c) whether the Government is aware that there is lack of basic amenities in the\nGovernment schools; and\n(d) the steps taken by the Government in this regard?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF EDUCATION\n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN)\n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n******\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 455 ANSWERED ON 03.04.2023 ASKED BY HON’BLE\nMP DR. KRISHNA PAL SINGH YADAV & PROF. RITA BAHUGUNA JOSHI\nREGARDING TEACHER-STUDENT RATIO AND BASIC AMENITIES IN\nGOVERNMENT SCHOOLS\n(a) and (b): The RTE Act, 2009 recognizes the importance of providing adequate\nnumber of teachers and lays down that the prescribed Pupil Teacher Ratio (PTR) to be\nmaintained for each school. The RTE Act, 2009 in its Schedule lays down Pupil-\nTeacher Ratio (PTR) for both primary and upper primary schools. At primary level, the\nPTR norm is 30:1 and at upper primary level, it is 35:1. As per UDISE 2021-22, at\nnational level, the PTR is 28:1 at primary level, 23:1 at upper primary level, which is\nbetter than prescribed norms.\nEducation is in the concurrent list of the Constitution and majority of the schools\nare under the domain of respective State and UT Governments. Advisories to maintain\nappropriate Pupil-Teacher Ratio (PTR) have also been issued to States and UTs from\ntime to time.\nThe National Education Policy (NEP), 2020, empowers teachers and places\nthem at the heart of the learning process through quality teacher education, recruitment,\ncontinuous professional development and positive working environment while ensuring\naccountability. As per NEP, 2020, National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE) has\nintroduced four year Integrated Teacher Education Programme (ITEP), on pilot basis, to\nequip teachers with enhanced curriculum and pedagogical knowledge. Similarly,\nNational Professional Standard for Teachers (NPST) for enhancing capabilities of\nteachers and National Mentoring Mission (NMM) for individual mentoring of school\nteachers by senior and retired teachers has been initiated.\nThe Department of School Education and Literacy has launched an integrated\nTeacher Training Programme called NISHTHA – National Initiative for School Heads\nand Teachers Holistic Advancement, on the DIKSHA platform, to improve learning\noutcomes at the elementary level. The NISHTHA programme has been further\nexpanded to NISHTHA 2.0 for secondary/senior secondary level teachers and\nNISHTHA 3.0 – Foundational Literacy and Numeracy (FLN) for teachers and school\nheads from pre-primary to class V.\n\n(c) and (d): Under Samagra Shiksha, the States and UTs are supported for\nstrengthening of existing government schools and for creation and augmentation of\ninfrastructure facilities based on the gaps determined from Unified District Information\nSystem for Education (UDISE+) and proposals received from respective State/UT. The\nneed for schools and also the infrastructural facilities in schools are worked out every\nyear by the respective State/Union Territory on incremental basis depending on their\nneed and priority and reflected in their Annual Work plan & Budget (AWP&B). These\nplans are then appraised and approved/estimated by the Project Approval Board (PAB)\nin the Department of School Education & Literacy in consultation with the States and\nUTs. The percentage of Government schools having infrastructure facilities is as follows:\nBoys\ntoilet\nGirls\ntoilet\nDrinking\nWater\nElectricity Playground Boundary\nwall\nLibrary Ramp\n95.5 97.4 98.24 88.89 72.6 67.43 91.3 82.2\nFurther, recently the Department of School Education & Literacy has approved a\nproject on Rejuvenation of Basic Infrastructure in approximately 1.20 lakh Government\nSchools across the country with an overall budget estimate of Rs. 4590 crore under\nSamagra Shiksha Scheme. The interventions covered under the project are major/minor\nrepairs, functional toilets (boys/girls), electricity connections, functional drinking water\nfacility and boundary walls.\n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_456": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS & FERTILIZERS\nDEPARTMENT OF CHEMICALS & PETROCHEMICALS\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUN-STARRED QUESTION NO. 456\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2023\n \nPCPIR in Andhra Pradesh\n456.     SHRI MARGANI BHARAT:\n            DR. BEESETTI VENKATA SATYAVATHI:\nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS, be pleased to state:\na\n. \nwhether it is true that a Petroleum, Chemicals and Petrochemical Investment\nRegion (PCPIR) was proposed to be established in Andhra Pradesh in 2009;\nb\n. \nif so, the details thereof;\nc\n. \nthe reasons for the delay in setting up this PCPIR in Andhra Pradesh;\nd\n. \nwhether the Government proposes to fast track the setting up of this PCPIR;\nand\ne\n. \nif so, the details thereof and if not, reasons therefor?\n \nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS\n(SHRI BHAGWANTH KHUBA)\n(a) to (b): \nYes, Sir. Government of India had approved setting up of Petroleum,\nChemicals and Petrochemicals Investment Region (PCPIR) in the state of Andhra\nPradesh (Vishakhapatnam-Kakinada region) in February, 2009.\n(c) The Master Plan was taken up by Vishakhapatnam PCPIR, Special\nDevelopment Authority and entrusted to M/s LEA Associates India on 15.03.2011.\nDetailed Draft Master Plan was published on 05.08.2013. Final incorporation of\nsuggestions and objections to the Draft Master Plan is in progress as per the\ndirections of Government of Andhra Pradesh.\n For Anchor tenant, Hindustan\nPetroleum Corporation Limited (HPCL) and GAIL have conducted pre-feasibility\nstudy but same is not yet ﬁnalized. On ﬁnalization of Anchor unit location,\nconﬁguration and capacity of the Cracker Complex etc., Master Plan will be\nfinalized and public hearing will be conducted for Environmental Clearance.\n(d) to (e) Govt. of A.P. has constituted VK-PCPIR-  Special Development Authority\n(SDA) vide G.O. Ms.NO.373 dated 24\nth\n  May 2008 for development activities of AP\nPCPIR including social infrastructure and housing, studying impact on the\nlivelihood of the people in the area and quality of life and environmental issues on\naccount of PCPIR. The PCPIR in Andhra Pradesh will be fast tracked once the\nAnchor tenant is finalised.\n****",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_457": "������������������� �\n������������������� �\n������������������������������ �\n������������������������������ ����\n���������������������������� �\nFake Currency \n������������������������������ �\n��������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������\n�\n������ �\n�\n���������������� �\n������������������������� �\n��������������� �����������������������������������������������\n�\n� �\n\nSTATEMENT REFFERED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 457 RAISED BY SHRI M. BADRUDDIN $-0$/\u000f\u0003 +21¶%/(\u0003\nMEMBER OF PARLIAMENT TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.04.2023 REGARDING \nFAKE CURRENCY \n�\n���� ���������\n�\n���� ��� �������������������� ������ �������� ������� ������� ������ ���� ������� ��� �����\n�����������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ����� ����� ����� ����� ����� �����\n������� ��� �������\n�����������\n����� ����� ����� ����� ����� �����\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������\n�\n����� ����� ����� ����� ����� �����\n����������������������� ������ ���� ���� ���� ����\n��������� ���� ������������ ��� ������������ ���� ������ ��������� ����������� ���� ��������������\n���������������������������������������������������� ������������������������������������\n��������� ��� ���� ������ ������ ��� ���� ������������ �������������������� ������� ��� ����\n���������������